From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 16 Sep 2026 20:05:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] device: reconnect a bonded LE device after a restart

A bonded LE peripheral is answered only while it sits on the kernel's accept
list: __hci_update_background_scan() runs the passive scan that picks up its
advertisements while hdev->pend_le_conns holds it, and that list is filled by
the MGMT Add Device command.

Nothing puts it back there when the daemon starts. load_devices() reads the
bond from storage and marks it non-temporary, but leaves auto connect off, and
every path into the connect list - att_connect_cb(), att_disconnected_cb() -
first tests device_get_auto_connect(). auto connect is turned on by Connect,
by Pair and by use, none of which run at start up, and it is not stored. So a
remote that is bonded, trusted and advertising is never connected until
something asks for it by hand.

Turn it on where the bearer is marked bonded. load_ltks() reaches here for
every stored LE bond as the adapter comes up, and so does a fresh pairing.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/src/device.c
+++ b/src/device.c
@@ -6962,6 +6962,15 @@
 
 	btd_device_set_temporary(device, false);
 
+	/* Put the peripheral back on the accept list. Reached from load_ltks()
+	 * for every stored bond as the adapter comes up, which is the one point
+	 * that runs both on a fresh bond and on every start; without it the
+	 * kernel is never asked to watch for the device and its advertisements
+	 * are ignored until something connects by hand.
+	 */
+	if (bdaddr_type != BDADDR_BREDR)
+		device_set_auto_connect(device, TRUE);
+
 	/* If the other bearer state was already true we don't need to
 	 * send any property signals.
 	 */
